00:21:42.060 --> 00:21:47.760
if anyone can price an answer it's Google and today's dip is the cost of

00:21:47.760 --> 00:21:54.860
moving first then the a realist reading an answer replaces the click and the

00:21:54.860 --> 00:22:00.760
click was the business. Fewer slots, cheaper early journey intent, a higher cost to serve.

00:22:01.320 --> 00:22:05.180
On that reading, the margin per query is thinner for good, not for a phase.

00:22:07.340 --> 00:22:13.240
Realists would point to how the language moved. Same rate for AI overviews in 2025,

00:22:13.760 --> 00:22:20.580
then lower monetization for AI mode now. Executives don't usually change wording like that

00:22:20.580 --> 00:22:27.460
unless the numbers make them then the market reading which is more about cash timing than

00:22:27.460 --> 00:22:32.740
technology the stock fell more than 10 percent in a quarter when cloud more than doubled

00:22:33.300 --> 00:22:38.260
investors seem to be pricing a capex bill that arrives before the ai revenue does

00:22:40.420 --> 00:22:47.300
there's a twist inside that reading cloud's 103 growth suggests the build out has customers

00:22:47.300 --> 00:22:54.300
paying rent on it. If that holds, search doesn't have to carry the whole bill.

00:22:54.300 --> 00:23:00.220
Partly, but some of those customers are AI labs that are hungry for cash themselves.

00:23:00.220 --> 00:23:05.420
This week Google was one of seven companies buying into Anthropics' $26 billion private

00:23:05.420 --> 00:23:13.100
placement alongside its IPO. That's a cloud provider putting equity into a lab that rents

00:23:13.100 --> 00:23:21.280
cloud compute. That's a fair hit on circular money, but an equity stake in a customer doesn't

00:23:21.280 --> 00:23:27.580
make the revenue fake. We'd need cloud's customer concentration before saying how much it matters.

00:23:29.320 --> 00:23:35.480
So where do these readings really part ways? On one variable, whether revenue per AI answer

00:23:35.480 --> 00:23:41.680
climbs back toward revenue per classic query. The AGI forward reading says yes, given time.

00:23:41.680 --> 00:23:44.460
The realist reading says it settles lower.

00:23:46.680 --> 00:23:49.600
And honestly, one quarter can't tell those two apart.

00:23:50.200 --> 00:23:52.200
Both predict exactly what we saw.

00:23:52.720 --> 00:23:54.620
That's why I keep resisting a verdict.

00:23:56.420 --> 00:23:58.820
Here's our read, held provisionally.

00:23:59.360 --> 00:24:05.060
We think this quarter weakens the idea that incumbents can comfortably fund the AI build-out out of search.

00:24:05.620 --> 00:24:11.540
Google's own AI product is cited as slowing its own growth, while CapEx runs ahead of cash.

00:24:11.680 --> 00:24:14.840
I'd put it more softly.

00:24:15.560 --> 00:24:22.200
Google still grew search 12% and earned $26.17 billion in net income this quarter.

00:24:22.740 --> 00:24:26.280
This is a margin story, not a solvency story.

00:24:28.280 --> 00:24:30.080
Agreed. Now the startups.

00:24:30.640 --> 00:24:34.300
If the best ad machine on the Internet earns less per AI answer,

00:24:34.760 --> 00:24:37.300
an ad-funded answer engine starts out worse.

00:24:37.300 --> 00:24:43.020
It has a thinner auction, fewer advertisers, and pays someone else's price for inference.

00:24:45.220 --> 00:24:48.860
Unless it picks queries where the answer sits right next to a transaction.

00:24:49.620 --> 00:24:52.280
Commerce, travel, a professional task.

00:24:52.780 --> 00:24:56.740
There you can charge per outcome or per seat instead of per ad shown.

00:24:58.660 --> 00:25:00.200
That's where we land, too.

00:25:00.740 --> 00:25:04.600
The room for ad-funded general search looks smaller than it did a year ago.

00:25:04.600 --> 00:25:11.060
The room for answers tied to a purchase, a subscription, or a workflow looks untouched by this quarter.

00:25:12.740 --> 00:25:17.660
There's a second group to think about. Companies that grow on Google traffic.

00:25:18.360 --> 00:25:24.520
If answers absorb the click, organic search becomes a less dependable way to acquire customers.

00:25:26.340 --> 00:25:29.080
One question worth exploring in diligence.

00:25:29.760 --> 00:25:31.540
What does the company earn per answer?

00:25:31.540 --> 00:25:36.940
What does each answer cost to serve, and how do both move as conversations get longer?

00:25:37.720 --> 00:25:42.220
Queries three times longer are good for engagement and can be bad for gross margin.

00:25:43.880 --> 00:25:51.440
And for a company that depends on search for growth, we'd want to see acquisition broken out by channel over several quarters.

00:25:52.240 --> 00:25:56.260
A blended customer acquisition cost hides exactly this shift.

00:25:56.260 --> 00:26:01.600
Where we still disagree. I think the gap is structural.

00:26:02.240 --> 00:26:07.220
An answer has less room for ads than a page of links, and I don't expect that to fully close.

00:26:08.940 --> 00:26:11.020
I think it's too early to call.

00:26:11.580 --> 00:26:17.380
This quarter carries currency and World Cup noise, and the global ads launched on earnings day.

00:26:17.900 --> 00:26:22.060
I'd want two more quarters of search revenue before calling anything structural.

00:26:23.920 --> 00:26:25.900
Three things would settle this.

00:26:26.260 --> 00:26:28.560
First, Alphabet's Q4 call.

00:26:29.260 --> 00:26:37.380
Annette Ashkenazi, the chief financial officer, said Google would provide further details on our Q4 call about 2027 CapEx.

00:26:39.000 --> 00:26:46.100
On that call, watch whether search picks up again once global AI mode ads have a full quarter behind them.

00:26:46.620 --> 00:26:53.080
If search revenue stays flat from one quarter to the next, the overtime claim gets much harder to defend.

00:26:53.080 --> 00:27:07.520
Second, disclosure. Does Google ever publish AI mode revenue per query or paid clicks and cost per click in its filings? Until it does, every revenue per answer number out there is a guess.

00:27:07.520 --> 00:27:10.760
Third, the cash.

00:27:11.300 --> 00:27:24.380
If 2027 CapEx goes past $300 billion, as CNBC reported is expected, and free cash flow stays negative, the funding question gets louder for everyone downstream.

00:27:26.240 --> 00:27:27.840
What would change our view?

00:27:28.380 --> 00:27:32.880
Two quarters where search growth holds up while AI mode's share of queries rises.

00:27:33.600 --> 00:27:35.980
That would show answers can be sold like links.

00:27:37.520 --> 00:27:43.520
And what would change mine is another flat quarter with clean comparisons and stable currency.

00:27:44.160 --> 00:27:47.200
At that point, I'd stop blaming the World Cup.

00:27:48.860 --> 00:27:52.000
That's the deep dive and today's AI briefing.

00:27:52.720 --> 00:28:00.700
Every source is linked in the show notes, and the AI briefing webpage has the written edition, this deep dive and every past episode.

00:28:01.240 --> 00:28:03.140
The daily briefing is back tomorrow.
